{%- comment -%}
  Shared markup is prepended to every view layout before rendering, so the
  assigns below are in scope for full/half_horizontal/half_vertical/quadrant.

  Polled responses (see settings.yml polling_url):
    IDX_0 = GET /rest/api/v2/users/me
    IDX_1 = GET /rest/api/v2/items?ql=...
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign me = IDX_0.data -%}
{%- assign items = IDX_1.data -%}
{%- assign total = IDX_1.pagination.total_items -%}

{%- comment -%}
  A failed poll yields {} rather than an exception, so an unreachable server
  or a rejected query would otherwise render as a silently blank screen. The
  device has no logs to check, so name the fault on the screen itself.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign fault = '' -%}
{%- unless me.id -%}
  {%- assign fault = 'Cannot reach Windshift. Check the server URL and API token.' -%}
{%- endunless -%}
{%- if fault == '' -%}
  {%- unless IDX_1.pagination -%}
    {%- assign fault = 'Windshift rejected the query. Check the QL syntax.' -%}
  {%- endunless -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%}
  Dates arrive as RFC 3339. Collapsing them to a YYYYMMDD integer makes the
  comparisons below unambiguous, and a missing due date lands on 0 — which is
  never "overdue", because every real date compares greater.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign today_num = 'now' | date: '%Y%m%d' | plus: 0 -%}

{%- assign overdue_count = 0 -%}
{%- assign due_today_count = 0 -%}
{%- for item in items -%}
  {%- assign due_num = item.due_date | date: '%Y%m%d' | plus: 0 -%}
  {%- if due_num > 0 -%}
    {%- if due_num < today_num -%}
      {%- assign overdue_count = overdue_count | plus: 1 -%}
    {%- elsif due_num == today_num -%}
      {%- assign due_today_count = due_today_count | plus: 1 -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}

{%- comment -%} "Stefan Ernst" -> "Stefan", falling back to the username. {%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign owner_name = me.first_name -%}
{%- if owner_name == blank -%}{%- assign owner_name = me.full_name | split: ' ' | first -%}{%- endif -%}
{%- if owner_name == blank -%}{%- assign owner_name = me.username -%}{%- endif -%}

{%- comment -%} Centred message, used for both the fault and empty states. {%- endcomment -%}
{% template notice %}
  <div class="layout layout--col layout--center">
    <span class="value value--small">{{ headline }}</span>
    <span class="label">{{ detail }}</span>
  </div>
{% endtemplate %}

{%- comment -%}
  One list row. {% render %} is scope-isolated, so every value it needs has to
  be passed in explicitly.
{%- endcomment -%}
{% template task_row %}
  {%- assign due_num = item.due_date | date: '%Y%m%d' | plus: 0 -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    The key rides in the label row rather than in .meta/.index — that slot is
    sized for a numeric rank, and a key like "WI-943" overflows it and lands
    on top of the title.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="item">
    <div class="content">
      <span class="title title--small" data-clamp="{{ clamp | default: 2 }}">{{ item.title }}</span>
      <div class="flex gap--small">
        <span class="label label--small">{{ item.key }}</span>
        {%- if item.status_name %}<span class="label label--small">{{ item.status_name }}</span>{% endif -%}
        {%- if item.priority_name %}<span class="label label--small">{{ item.priority_name }}</span>{% endif -%}
        {%- if due_num > 0 -%}
          {%- if due_num < today_num -%}
            <span class="label label--small label--underline">Overdue {{ item.due_date | date: '%b %-d' }}</span>
          {%- elsif due_num == today_num -%}
            <span class="label label--small label--underline">Due today</span>
          {%- else -%}
            <span class="label label--small">Due {{ item.due_date | date: '%b %-d' }}</span>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
{% endtemplate %}
